From: timstarr@netcom.com (Tim Starr)
Date: Tue, 25 Oct 1994 23:31:54 -0700
Subject: [#94-10-510] Generation X

Another couple of sources worth looking into are "Generations: The History
of America's Future," by Strauss & Howe, and "Generation X: Abort? Retry?
Fail?" by the same authors, although I haven't read the latter.  The former
elaborates their cyclical theory of history: there are 4 different kinds
of generations, which repeat each other in roughly the same order, although
one kind may get skipped now and then.  Among the fascinating implications
of their theory is that the same arrangement between generations that
produced both the Glorious Revolution in England in 1688 and the American
Revolution in 1776 is about to come up again right around 2004-5.  Ready?

